SECTION I — Transaction Lifecycle and Workflow Transitions
Every transactional entity (JOURNAL_ENTRY, SALES_INVOICE, PURCHASE_BILL, PAYMENT, TAX_FILING, PAYROLL_RUN, STOCK_ADJUSTMENT) follows the canonical state machine in src/server/routes/journey.ts:
code
Code
[ Create ]
                     │
                     ▼
                 ┌────────┐
        ┌───────▶│ DRAFT  │◀───────┐
        │        └────┬───┘        │
        │             │ (Submit)   │
        │             ▼            │
        │     ┌───────────────┐    │
        │     │   SUBMITTED   │    │
        │     └───────┬───────┘    │
        │             │ (Review)   │
        │             ▼            │
        │     ┌───────────────┐    │ (Return for
        │     │ UNDER_REVIEW  │    │  Correction)
        │     └───────┬───────┘    │
(Reject)│        ┌────┴────┐       │
        ├────────┘         └───────┤
        │                          │
        ▼                          ▼
   ┌──────────┐              ┌────────────┐
   │ REJECTED │              │  RETURNED  │
   └──────────┘              └────────────┘
        │
        │ (Approve - Validates Role, Scope, Limit, SoD)
        ▼
   ┌──────────┐
   │ APPROVED │
   └────┬─────┘
        │ (Post to General Ledger)
        ▼
   ┌──────────┐
   │  POSTED  │  (IMMUTABLE ACCOUNTING RECORD)
   └────┬─────┘
        │ (Reverse - Generates Reversing Double-Entry JE)
        ▼
   ┌──────────┐
   │ REVERSED │  (Never silently erased; links to Reversal JE)
   └──────────┘

Controlled Operational Transitions:
- CANCELLED: Pre-post cancellation with mandatory reason.
- ARCHIVED: Preserved outside active listings.
- SOFT_DELETED: Draft removal with complete audit trail.
- RESTORED: Recovered to DRAFT status.
- COPY: Clones existing record into a new DRAFT.
Transition Authority & Guard Rules
DRAFT: Editable by Preparer (Bookkeeper, Accountant, Company Administrator, Company Owner).
SUBMITTED / UNDER_REVIEW: Locked against edits. Visible in Approver's inbox (/activity-center?workspace=approvals).
RETURNED / REJECTED: Re-opened for editing by preparer. Mandatory rejection/return remark recorded.
APPROVED: Requires approve permission, sufficient PHP monetary limit (approvalLimitCentavos), and Segregation of Duties (approver cannot approve own created or edited transaction).
POSTED: Completely immutable. Cannot be edited or deleted. Corrections require REVERSE (reverseJournalEntry), creating an offsetting journal and an adjusted draft.
