SECTION M — Existing Security Restrictions
Company Owner Protection:
Company Administrator and other non-owner roles CANNOT edit, disable, demote, remove, or revoke permissions of a Company Owner (403 OWNER_PROTECTION_VIOLATION).
The last active Company Owner cannot be removed, disabled, or demoted (400 LAST_OWNER_PROTECTION).
Account & Membership Lockout:
Disabled accounts (status !== 'ACTIVE') or removed company members (membershipStatus === 'REMOVED') are immediately blocked on login and bearer session validation (403 ACCOUNT_DISABLED / 403 MEMBERSHIP_REMOVED), returning 0 modules, 0 submodules, 0 actions.
General Ledger Immutability:
Posted journal entries (status === 'POSTED') cannot be modified or deleted directly. They must be corrected through formal reversal journals (reverseJournalEntry).
Accounting Period Hard Lock:
Transactions dated on or before companies.lockDate or within a closed accounting_periods row are strictly rejected with 400 PERIOD_LOCKED.
Segregation of Duties (SoD):
Approvers cannot approve transactions they personally prepared (canApproveOwnCreatedTransactions = false) or edited (canApproveOwnEditedTransactions = false).
Preparer roles (Bookkeeper) cannot be assigned transaction approval authority (Approver) without triggering ROLE_COMPATIBILITY_PROHIBITED.
Auditor role is strictly read-only and prohibited from combining with operational write roles.
